#Project requeriments: 
Backend Engineer Challenge
(We give you 72hs to complete and return)

We are looking for a Backend Engineer who can build a secure, high-performance data
pipeline on Google Cloud. Your goal is to transform "messy" ultrasound PDFs into
structured, actionable JSON data.
👉 The Challenge: Cloud-Native PDF Processing
Build a REST API that automates the extraction and storage of medical ultrasound
reports. You must use Google Cloud Services for the core infrastructure.
The Workflow:
1. Secure Ingestion: An endpoint to upload PDF reports.
2. Extraction Engine: Use a document OCR, form parser or Google Cloud
Document AI to extract: Patient, Owner, Veterinarian, Diagnosis, and
Recommendations.
3. Image Asset Management: Extract images from the PDF and store them in
Google Cloud Storage (GCS).
4. Database & API: Store the structured metadata in a database (e.g., Cloud SQL
or Firestore) and provide a GET endpoint to retrieve the json and don't forget the
images.
📩 Deliverables:
● The Code: Public GitHub repository with a clear README.md.
● The Live API: A hosted endpoint (e.g., running on Cloud Run or App Engine).
● The Technical Walkthrough (5 min video):
○ Show a demo of the API in action (using Postman or cURL).
○ Explain your architectural choices regarding GCP services.

💡 Evaluation Criteria:
We will evaluate your submission based on four pillars of cloud engineering:
authentication, scalability, security and usage of GCP services.

#Architecture decisions 
**Endpoints**

For a firts version, i will create the two basic endpoint. One POST endpoint to upload the pdf. And one GET endpoint to retrive the json and the images. 

In this firts version, the proccess will be a synchronous proccess. 

If i have time, i can do a asynchronous proccess and add another endpoint like:

- GET /reports/{id}/status
- GET /reports
- DELETE /reports/{id}

For the images, i gonna pass the url’s GCP images on the json. 

**OCR options**

I need to use Document AI. It have a ia tool, so i can extract the data in best way. It is useful becouse it have ability to extract informactio from diferent formats.  

**Data Base**

For the data base i will use Firestore. Is the Google Cloud NoSQL option. 

<aside>
💡

"Elegí Firestore sobre Cloud SQL por tres razones:

1. Escalabilidad: Firestore escala automáticamente de 0 a millones
de documentos sin intervención, mientras SQL requiere gestión manual.
2. Modelo de datos: Mi estructura es naturalmente un documento JSON,
no necesito JOINs ni relaciones complejas.
3. Serverless: Cero gestión de infraestructura, backups automáticos,
y free tier generoso que cubre el proyecto completamente.

Para casos con transacciones complejas o queries analíticos,
evaluaría Cloud SQL o BigQuery."

</aside>

**Data Base Schema**

```jsx
// Collection: reports

{
  // Identificadores
  "id": "report_abc123",
  "created_at": "2025-02-02T14:30:00Z",
  "status": "completed",
  
  // CAMPOS REQUERIDOS POR EL CHALLENGE
  "patient": "Chester",
  "owner": "Naveda", 
  "veterinarian": "MV. Martin Vittaz",
  "diagnosis": "Imágenes sugerentes de osteosarcoma en húmero derecho",
  "recommendations": "Control radiológico en 30 días",
  
  // Archivos (parte del challenge)
  "images": [
    {
      "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/bucket/img1.jpg",
      "filename": "image_1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/bucket/img2.jpg", 
      "filename": "image_2.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
```

